// OPEN DEFECT, kept as its smallest reproducer; no test asserts it. A sealed room with a free-standing fin 0.012 units
// thick (x 0..0.012, y -64..64, z 64..160). The fin is a whole brush thinner than 0.02 units: its side planes would cut
// the 0.012 slab it lies in by a winding thinner than 0.02, which SplitBrush and CheckSplitBrush refuse, so the slab is
// one leaf from wall to wall and floor to ceiling. The middle of that leaf is inside the fin, so all of it is solid: a
// sheet that divides the room, and the half the player is not in is then filled as unreachable (half the room's air
// reads solid in hull 0; no leak, exit 0). This is not LeafNode's rule: the build without it does the same. 0.18.1 is
// correct; 2.0.0-alpha11 and releases 1.4502/1.4505 leave a smaller block of solid beside the fin. At 0.0201 units the
// fin is carved and the room is right (the 0.06 fin of q1_brushbsp_leaf_guard_keeps_material.map is tested).
